So, what are the large language models?

95
00:10:02,606 --> 00:10:13,472
Large language models like ChatGPT 4, Generative Pre-trained Transformer 4, O, and Google Gemini are sophisticated AI systems designed to comprehend and generate human-like text.

96
00:10:13,552 --> 00:10:18,752
These models are built using deep learning techniques and are trained on vast datasets collected from the internet.

97
00:10:19,054 --> 00:10:27,492
They leverage self-attention mechanisms to analyze the relationship between words or tokens, allowing them to capture context and produce coherent relevant responses.

98
00:10:27,822 --> 00:10:36,752
LLMs have significant applications, including powering virtual assistant, chat boards, content creation, language translation, and supporting research and decision making.

99
00:10:36,832 --> 00:10:44,272
Their ability to generate fluent and contextually appropriate text has advanced natural language processing and improved human-computer interaction.

100
00:10:44,398 --> 00:10:47,072
So now let's see what are large language models used for.

101
00:10:47,312 --> 00:10:53,392
Large language models are utilized in scenarios with limited or no domain-specific data available for training.

102
00:10:53,552 --> 00:11:05,712
These scenarios include both few short and zero short training approaches, which rely on the model's strong inductive bias and its capability to derive meaningful representation from a small amount of data or even no data at all.

103
00:11:05,872 --> 00:11:08,592
So now let's see how large language models are trained.

104
00:11:08,832 --> 00:11:18,672
Large language models typically undergo pre-training on a board, all encompassing data set that shares statical similarities with the dataset specific to the target task.

105
00:11:18,832 --> 00:11:27,392
The objective of pre-training is to enable the model to acquire high-level features that can later be applied during the fine-tuning phase for specific tasks.

106
00:11:27,552 --> 00:11:31,632
So there are some training processes of LLM which involves several steps.

107
00:11:31,792 --> 00:11:33,632
The first one is text preprocessing.

108
00:11:33,712 --> 00:11:38,672
The textual data is transformed into a numerical representation that the LLM model can effectively process.

109
00:11:38,832 --> 00:11:43,712
This conversion may involve techniques like tokenization encoding and creating input sequences.

110
00:11:43,872 --> 00:11:46,032
The second one is random parameter initialization.

111
00:11:46,192 --> 00:11:49,792
The model's parameters are initialized randomly before the training process begins.

112
00:11:49,902 --> 00:11:51,632
The third one is input numerical data.

113
00:11:51,792 --> 00:11:55,632
The numerical representation of the text data is fed into the model of processing.

114
00:11:55,758 --> 00:12:03,312
The model's architecture, typically based on transformers, allows it to capture the contextual relationship between the words or tokens in the next.

115
00:12:03,406 --> 00:12:05,232
The fourth one is loss function calculation.

116
00:12:05,422 --> 00:12:11,716
A loss function calculation measures the discrepancy between the model's prediction and the actual next word or token in a syntax.

117
00:12:12,014 --> 00:12:15,300
The LLM model aims to minimize this loss during training.

118
00:12:15,534 --> 00:12:17,312
The fifth one is parameter optimization.

119
00:12:17,454 --> 00:12:20,420
The model's parameters are adjusted through optimization technique.

120
00:12:20,512 --> 00:12:26,112
This involves calculating gradient and updating the parameters accordingly, gradually improving the model's performance.

121
00:12:26,286 --> 00:12:27,844
The last one is iterative training.

122
00:12:27,982 --> 00:12:37,712
The training process is repeated over multiple iterations or epochs until the model's output achieve a satisfactory level of accuracy on that given task or dataset.

123
00:12:37,872 --> 00:12:47,588
By following this training process, large language models learn to capture linguistic patterns, understand context, and generate coherent responses, enabling them to excel at various language related tasks.

124
00:12:47,792 --> 00:12:50,992
The next topic is how do large language models work?

125
00:12:51,278 --> 00:12:57,392
So, large language models leverage deep neural networks to generate output based on patterns learned from the training data.

126
00:12:57,552 --> 00:13:06,628
Typically, a large language model adopts a transformer architecture which enables the model to identify the relationship between words in a sentence irrespective of their position in the sequence.

127
00:13:07,008 --> 00:13:15,968
In contrast to RNNs that rely on recurrence to capture token relationships, transform a neural network, employ self-attention as their primary mechanism.

128
00:13:16,142 --> 00:13:26,436
Self-attention calculates attention scores that determine the importance of each token with respect to the other token in the text sequence, facilitating the modeling of intricate relationship within the data.

