01:10:53,614 --> 01:10:57,700
The first one is Generative Adversarial Networks GANs.

694
01:10:58,256 --> 01:11:00,580
The artist versus the critic game.

695
01:11:01,134 --> 01:11:02,180
So how it works?

696
01:11:02,734 --> 01:11:06,916
Think of GANs like competition between the two neural networks.

697
01:11:07,566 --> 01:11:11,616
The generator is like a rookie artist trying to create a fake art.

698
01:11:11,790 --> 01:11:16,548
The discriminator is the tough critic trying to tell the real art from the fake.

699
01:11:17,216 --> 01:11:19,696
So the artist creates random images.

700
01:11:19,936 --> 01:11:25,296
The critic says fake or real and the artist learns to get better.

701
01:11:25,550 --> 01:11:30,788
So over the time the fake images become indistinguishable from the real ones.

702
01:11:31,630 --> 01:11:34,816
So there is a real world analogy.

703
01:11:35,216 --> 01:11:43,076
It's like a student that is a generator forging a signature and a teacher discriminator spotting it.

704
01:11:43,376 --> 01:11:47,332
As both improve, the forgeries become nearly perfect.

705
01:11:48,078 --> 01:11:49,828
