3325
05:09:30,638 --> 05:09:32,836
So, what exactly is Langchain?

3326
05:09:33,870 --> 05:09:48,388
Langchain is an open source framework designed to help developers build applications powered by large language models by providing tools and abstractions to simplify the process of integrating LLMs with external data sources and workflows.

3327
05:09:48,816 --> 05:09:56,896
Now, imagine you're building an AI application where an LLM model like GPT 4 is needed to generate an initial response to your query.

3328
05:09:57,646 --> 05:10:01,380
Lama 3 or other versions to refine that response.

3329
05:10:01,680 --> 05:10:11,760
A custom-built AI agent to decide whether it can answer the query without a hiccup or if it has to fetch external sources to generate a response.

3330
05:10:12,000 --> 05:10:16,800
Most importantly, a solid memory to store all previous user interactions.

3331
05:10:17,006 --> 05:10:22,980
Without Langchain, managing all these components manually would require extensive coding.

3332
05:10:23,374 --> 05:10:38,596
You need to write a custom code snippet to handle API calls to your LLM like GPT, Lama, create and maintain a dedicated memory space and most importantly, a fully customized decision-making capable AI agent.

3333
05:10:38,926 --> 05:10:44,880
Yet in scenarios where you can see an opportunity to scale it up, the possibilities are questionable.

3334
05:10:45,120 --> 05:10:49,604
This approach leads to a lot of boilerplate code and makes the system complex.

3335
05:10:50,094 --> 05:10:58,276
Langchain simplifies this by providing an open source framework that helps developers build applications powered by large language models.

3336
05:10:58,702 --> 05:11:04,868
It enables training prompts, interacting with external data, and adding memory for contextual understanding.

3337
05:11:05,294 --> 05:11:08,196
Now, let's discuss some of the key features of Langchain.

3338
05:11:08,494 --> 05:11:09,860
Firstly, LLM support.

3339
05:11:10,080 --> 05:11:16,804
It works with both closed source GPT-4 and open source models like Lama 3 with simple API integrations.

3340
05:11:17,294 --> 05:11:18,276
Prompt templates.

3341
05:11:18,606 --> 05:11:22,756
It allows dynamic prompt customization instead of hard-coding queries.

3342
05:11:23,246 --> 05:11:24,260
Third one is chains.

3343
05:11:24,480 --> 05:11:31,876
It helps connect multiple tasks like querying and LLM retrieving data and processing responses in a seamless workflow.

3344
05:11:32,302 --> 05:11:38,640
Fourth one is indexes, supports document loaders and vector databases to pull in external data.

3345
05:11:38,958 --> 05:11:40,100
First one is memory.

3346
05:11:40,430 --> 05:11:45,188
It enables applications to retain past interactions, improving contextual awareness.

3347
05:11:45,582 --> 05:11:46,692
And lastly, the agents.

3348
05:11:47,118 --> 05:11:52,260
It uses LLMs as reasoning engines to dynamically decide the next step in the workflow.

3349
05:11:52,622 --> 05:11:59,172
With Langchain, developers can efficiently build AI-powered applications without reinventing the wheel.

