4613
07:10:12,224 --> 07:10:13,597
So now what is RNN?

4614
07:10:14,224 --> 07:10:18,724
RNN are a type of neural network that are designed to process sequential data.

4615
07:10:19,024 --> 07:10:24,708
They can analyze data with temporal dimensions such as time series, speech, and text.

4616
07:10:25,344 --> 07:10:30,276
RNN can do this by using a hidden state passed from one timestamp to the next.

4617
07:10:30,544 --> 07:10:36,624
The next hidden state is updated at each other time step based on the input and the previous hidden state.

4618
07:10:36,878 --> 07:10:46,308
RNN are able to capture short-term dependencies in sequential data, but they struggle with capturing long-term dependencies while the LSTMs are made.

4619
07:10:46,944 --> 07:10:50,404
So moving forward, let's discuss types of LSTM gates.

4620
07:10:51,344 --> 07:10:58,052
So LSTM models have three types of gates the input gate, the forget gate, and the output gate.

4621
07:10:58,944 --> 07:11:02,052
So let's first discuss the input gate.

4622
07:11:02,446 --> 07:11:07,588
The input gate controls the flow of information into the memory cell deciding what to store.

4623
07:11:08,144 --> 07:11:13,028
The input gate determines which values from the input should be updated in the memory cell.

4624
07:11:13,344 --> 07:11:22,308
It uses a sigmoid activation function to scale the values between 0 and 1 and then applies point-wise multiplication to decide what information to store.

4625
07:11:22,784 --> 07:11:24,452
Next is forget gate.

4626
07:11:24,910 --> 07:11:29,508
Controls the flow of information out of the memory cell, deciding what to discard.

4627
07:11:30,030 --> 07:11:34,212
The forget gate decides what information should be discarded from the memory cell.

4628
07:11:34,384 --> 07:11:43,204
It also uses a sigmoid activation function to scale the values between 0 and 1, followed by 0.5 multiplication to determine what information to forget.

4629
07:11:43,744 --> 07:11:45,636
The last one is output gate.

4630
07:11:46,064 --> 07:11:51,268
Controls the flow of information out of the LSTM, deciding what to use for the output.

4631
07:11:51,726 --> 07:11:54,660
The output gate determines the output of the LSTM unit.

4632
07:11:54,944 --> 07:12:03,364
It uses a sigmoid activation function to scale the values from 0 to 1, then applies 0.5 multiplication to produce the output of the LSTM unit.

4633
07:12:03,662 --> 07:12:08,304
So these gates implemented using sigmoid function, are trained using backpropagation.

4634
07:12:08,526 --> 07:12:18,864
They open and close based on the input and the previous hidden state, allowing the LSTM to selectively retain or discard information, effectively capturing long-term dependencies.

4635
07:12:19,150 --> 07:12:21,636
So now let's discuss application of LSTM.

4636
07:12:22,446 --> 07:12:32,036
LSTM models are highly effective and used in various applications, including video analysis, analyzing video frames to identify action, object, and scenes.

4637
07:12:32,494 --> 07:12:38,276
The second is language simulation, tasks like language modeling, machine translation, and text summarization.

4638
07:12:38,798 --> 07:12:40,676
The third one is time series prediction.

4639
07:12:41,024 --> 07:12:43,492
So predicting future values in a time series.

4640
07:12:44,494 --> 07:12:46,020
The fourth is voice recognition.

4641
07:12:46,414 --> 07:12:50,052
Tasks such as speech to text transcription and command recognition.

4642
07:12:51,054 --> 07:12:56,464
The last one is sentiment analysis, classifying text sentiment as positive, negative on URL.

4643
07:12:56,704 --> 07:12:58,784
So there are many more examples of LSTM.

4644
07:12:58,864 --> 07:13:03,204
So now let's move forward and understand LSTM model and how it works with example.

4645
07:13:03,504 --> 07:13:06,628
Let's consider the task of predicting the next word in a sentence.

4646
07:13:06,958 --> 07:13:10,340
This is a common application of LSTM networks in natural language processing.

4647
07:13:10,704 --> 07:13:17,824
So I will break it down step by step using the analogy of remembering a story and deciding what comes next based on the context.

4648
07:13:17,904 --> 07:13:19,664
So imagine you are reading a story.

4649
07:13:19,824 --> 07:13:25,092
As you read, you need to remember what has happened so far to predict what might happen next.

4650
07:13:25,518 --> 07:13:28,384
So let's illustrate with a simple example center.

4651
07:13:28,864 --> 07:13:30,852
The cat sat on the dash.

4652
07:13:31,246 --> 07:13:35,588
So you want to predict the next word, which could be mat or roof or something else.

4653
07:13:36,177 --> 07:13:43,332
And LSTM network helps this make prediction by remembering important parts of the story and forgetting irrelevant details.

4654
07:13:43,598 --> 07:13:45,796
So now let's dive into step by step process.

4655
07:13:45,998 --> 07:13:48,452
So step by step acclimation using LSTM.

4656
07:13:48,544 --> 07:13:51,104
The first one is reading the story, input sequence.

4657
07:13:51,264 --> 07:13:55,876
As you read each word in the word sentence, you process it and store relevant information.

4658
07:13:56,078 --> 07:14:03,300
For example, the you understand its determiner, cat, you know it's a noun and the subject of the sentence.

4659
07:14:03,744 --> 07:14:07,076
Set indicates the action performed by the subject.

4660
07:14:07,504 --> 07:14:11,716
On preposition indicating the relationship between the cat and the next noun.

4661
07:14:11,984 --> 07:14:16,544
So this sequence diagram showing the words being read and processed.

4662
07:14:16,878 --> 07:14:18,436
So second comes forget gate.

4663
07:14:18,798 --> 07:14:22,864
As you move through the sentence, you might decide that some details are no longer important.

4664
07:14:23,150 --> 07:14:29,184
For instance, you might decide that knowing the is less important now that you have get and set.

4665
07:14:30,030 --> 07:14:34,116
So the word forget gate help discard this less important information.

4666
07:14:34,510 --> 07:14:39,684
So this sequence diagram you can see on the screen showing how relevant information is discarded.

4667
07:14:40,302 --> 07:14:42,084
So the third one, input gate.

4668
07:14:42,958 --> 07:14:48,068
When you read on, you need to decide how relevant this information is.

4669
07:14:48,558 --> 07:14:54,788
So this sequence diagram in the screen is showing how new information is integrated with the last one.

4670
07:14:55,952 --> 07:14:58,756
the fourth one is the cell state memory part.

4671
07:14:58,992 --> 07:15:01,764
So this is like your memory of the story so far.

4672
07:15:02,032 --> 07:15:05,988
It carries information about the subject cat and the action set on.

4673
07:15:06,254 --> 07:15:09,636
So it updates the new information as you read each word.

4674
07:15:10,672 --> 07:15:14,752
the cat set on the retaining the important context.

4675
07:15:14,912 --> 07:15:18,832
So this sequence diagram showing how the memory is updated with the new information.

4676
07:15:19,086 --> 07:15:20,548
So the last one is output gate.

4677
07:15:21,294 --> 07:15:27,268
When you need to predict the next word, the output gate helps you decide based on the current memory, cell state.

4678
07:15:27,630 --> 07:15:30,532
So it uses the context, the cat set on the.

4679
07:15:31,278 --> 07:15:38,116
So the predict the next word might be mat because cat and mat are often associated with the context.

4680
07:15:38,752 --> 07:15:44,992
So it can predict anything, the cat sat on the table or on the sofa, anything.

4681
07:15:45,232 --> 07:15:51,364
But mat, why I'm saying mat because cat and mat are often associated in the same context.

4682
07:15:51,792 --> 07:15:56,132
So this diagram is showing the prediction of the next word based on the current memory.

4683
07:15:56,462 --> 07:16:03,396
So there are many applications where you can use LSTM in predicting time series or next word in the sentence.

4684
07:16:03,792 --> 07:16:09,700
So by the using of LSTM gates, input gate, forget gate, and output gate, and updating the cell state.

4685
07:16:09,872 --> 07:16:16,804
The network can predict the next word in a sequence by maintaining relevant context and discarding unnecessary information.

